1. Docker installation and basic commands
    Command	                                      Description
docker --version	                    Displays the installed Docker version.
docker version	                      Displays Docker client and server versions.
docker info	                          Displays Docker system information.
sudo systemctl start docker	          Starts the Docker service.
sudo systemctl stop docker	          Stops the Docker service.
sudo systemctl restart docker	        Restarts the Docker service.
sudo systemctl status docker	        Checks whether Docker is running.
sudo systemctl enable docker	        Starts Docker automatically at boot.

2. Docker image commands
A Docker image is a template used to create a container.
    Command	                                      Description
docker images	                        Lists all locally available images.
docker pull nginx	                    Downloads the NGINX image.
docker pull ubuntu	                  Downloads the Ubuntu image.
docker build -t myapp .	              Builds an image from a Dockerfile.
docker tag myapp myapp:v1	            Assigns a version tag to an image.
docker rmi myapp	                    Removes a Docker image.
docker image inspect nginx	          Displays detailed image information.

3. Docker container commands
A container is a running instance of a Docker image.
Command	                                                  Description
docker run hello-world	                          Runs the Hello World container.
docker run -it ubuntu bash	                      Starts Ubuntu interactively with a shell.
docker run -d nginx	                              Runs NGINX in the background.
docker run --name web nginx	                      Creates a container named web.
docker run -d -p 8080:80 nginx	                  Maps host port 8080 to container port 80.
docker ps	                                        Lists running containers.
docker ps -a	                                    Lists all containers, including stopped ones.
docker start web	                                Starts a stopped container.
docker stop web	                                  Stops a running container.
docker restart web	                              Restarts a container.
docker rm web	                                    Removes a stopped container.
docker rm -f web	                                Forcefully removes a container.
docker logs web	                                  Displays container logs.
docker exec -it web bash	                        Opens a shell inside a running container.
docker inspect web	                              Displays detailed container information

4. Dockerfile instructions
A Dockerfile is a text file containing instructions to build a Docker image.
Instruction	                                                Description
FROM	                                                Specifies the base image.
WORKDIR	                                              Sets the working directory inside the image.
COPY	                                                Copies files from host to image.
ADD	                                                  Copies files and can extract local archives.
RUN	                                                  Executes commands while building the image.
CMD	                                                  Specifies the default command when a container starts.
ENTRYPOINT	                                          Specifies the main executable of the container.
EXPOSE	                                              Documents the port used by the application.
ENV	                                                  Sets an environment variable.
ARG	                                                  Defines a variable available during image building.
USER	                                                Specifies the user to run commands as.
VOLUME	                                              Declares a mount point for persistent data.

FROM python:3.12
WORKDIR /app
COPY app.py .
CMD ["python", "app.py"]

docker build -t python-hello .
docker run python-hello
(docker build creates the image, and docker run executes it.)

5. Docker networking commands
Docker networking allows containers to communicate with each other.
Command	                                                         Description
docker network ls	                                      Lists Docker networks.
docker network create mynet	                            Creates a network named mynet.
docker network inspect mynet	                          Displays network details.
docker network connect mynet web	                      Connects a container to a network.
docker network disconnect mynet web	                    Disconnects a container from a network.
docker network rm mynet	                                Removes a network.

Connect two containers
docker network create mynet
Creates a network.
docker run -d --name web --network mynet nginx
Runs NGINX inside the network.
docker run -it --network mynet busybox sh
Starts BusyBox inside the same network.
Inside BusyBox:
ping web
Tests communication with the NGINX container using its name.

6. Docker volume commands
A Docker volume stores data outside the container's writable layer so that the data can persist when a container is removed.
Command	                                                            Description
docker volume ls	                                        Lists Docker volumes.
docker volume create myvol	                              Creates a volume.
docker volume inspect myvol	                              Displays volume details.
docker volume rm myvol	                                  Removes a volume.
docker volume prune	                                      Removes unused volumes.


Mount a volume
docker volume create myvol
Creates a volume.
docker run -it --name c1 -v myvol:/data ubuntu bash
Mounts the volume at /data inside Ubuntu.
Inside the container:
cd /data
echo "Hello Docker" > file.txt
exit
Creates a file in the mounted volume.
docker run --rm -v myvol:/data ubuntu cat /data/file.txt
Reads the same file from another container, demonstrating persistent data.

7. DockerHub commands
DockerHub is a cloud-based registry used to store and share Docker images.
Command	                                                     Description
docker login	                                            Logs in to DockerHub.
docker logout	                                            Logs out from DockerHub.
docker tag myapp USERNAME/myapp:v1	                      Tags an image for DockerHub.
docker push USERNAME/myapp:v1	                            Uploads an image to DockerHub.
docker pull USERNAME/myapp:v1	                            Downloads an image from DockerHub.

Practical example
docker login
docker build -t myapp .
docker tag myapp USERNAME/myapp:v1
docker push USERNAME/myapp:v1
(This builds an image, tags it with your DockerHub username, and uploads it.)

