9. Java Hello World using Docker
The syllabus requires running Hello World using a Java container.

Create HelloWorld.java:
class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello World");
    }
}


Dockerfile:
FROM openjdk:17
WORKDIR /app
COPY HelloWorld.java .
RUN javac HelloWorld.java
CMD ["java", "HelloWorld"]

Commands:
docker build -t java-hello .
docker run java-hello

- docker build builds the Java image.
- docker run executes the Java program.


