11. Docker with MySQL
Your syllabus requires demonstrating container networking and volumes by connecting an application with MySQL.
Start MySQL container
docker run -d \
  --name mysql \
  -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=root123 \
  -e MYSQL_DATABASE=testdb \
  -p 3306:3306 \
  mysql:8


Option	Description
-d	Runs in the background.
--name mysql	Names the container.
-e	Sets an environment variable.
-p 3306:3306	Maps MySQL port.
mysql:8	Specifies the MySQL image.

Check container:
docker ps
docker logs mysql

Connect to MySQL:
docker exec -it mysql mysql -uroot -p

Inside MySQL:
SHOW DATABASES;
USE testdb;

- SHOW DATABASES displays databases.
- USE testdb selects the database.
